+            // Only reject if we ask for letters but there are no letters in the range,
+            // OR if we ask for digits but there are no digits in the range.
+            // When asking for both letters and digits, it's acceptable to have only one type available.
+            // The check should be: if we ask for letters (letters=true) AND end <= ASCII_A (65), 
+            // then there are no letters in [start, end). Similarly for digits.
+            // However, the original bug was that this check was backwards - it was checking
+            // whether we ask for something but it's not available, when it should be checking
+            // whether we ask for something and there is NO way to get it.
+            if ((letters && end <= ASCII_A) || (digits && end <= ASCII_0)) {
